.SH ENCODE-DASHCAM
.sp
Batch encode dashcam footage, merging rear and front camera footage.
.sp
This command\(aqs defaults are intended for use with Red Tiger dashcam output and file structure.
.sp
The rear camera view will be placed in the bottom right of the video scaled by dividing the
width and height by the \fB\-\-rear\-view\-scale\-divisor\fP value specified. It will also be cropped
using the \fB\-\-rear\-crop\fP value unless \fB\-\-no\-rear\-crop\fP is passed.
.sp
Files are automatically grouped using the regular expression passed with
\fB\-M\fP/\fB\-\-match\-regexp\fP\&. This RE must contain at least one group and only the first group will
be considered. Make dubious use of non\-capturing groups if necessary. The captured group string
is expected to be usable with the time format specified with \fB\-\-time\-format\fP (see
\fBstrptime\fP documentation at
\X'tty: link https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime.strptime'\fI\%https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime.strptime\fP\X'tty: link').
.sp
Front and rear files are paired by timestamp proximity (within \fB\-\-max\-offset\fP seconds). Files
without a corresponding partner are logged and skipped without deletion.
.sp
Original files whose content is successfully converted are sent to the wastebin.
.sp
Example use:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
encode\-dashcam Movie_F/ Movie_R/ ~/output_dir
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
