.SS list\-flags
.sp
List the state of every \fIchrome://flags\fP entry the browser has been told about.
.sp
Flag titles and descriptions are not stored in the profile. They are read out of the installed
browser binary when one can be found, and otherwise fetched from the Chromium source at the tag
matching the installed browser version. Either way the result is cached. Flags the profile
still records but the browser no longer defines are shown with an empty description.
.sp
A binary supplies no owners or expiry milestones, so those are filled in from
\fIflag\-metadata.json\fP unless \fI\-\-offline\fP was given.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
chrome\-dump list\-flags [OPTIONS]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-all
Include flags left at their default.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-search <search>
Only show flags whose name, title, or description matches.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-binary <binary>
Browser binary to read the flag table out of.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Never fetch; use only the cache and the binary.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
