.SS preferences
.sp
Show a profile\(aqs settings the way the browser\(aqs own settings page groups them.
.sp
Chrome only writes a preference once it differs from its built\-in default, so the summary also
reports the defaults that are in force and marks where each value came from. It is lossy: use
\fI\-\-expand\fP for every stored key, \fI\-\-raw\fP for the file as stored, or \fI\-\-key\fP for one value.
.sp
\fI\-\-secure\fP reads \fISecure Preferences\fP, which holds no settings the summary knows about, so it
implies \fI\-\-raw\fP unless \fI\-\-expand\fP is given.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
chrome\-dump preferences [OPTIONS]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-changed
Omit settings left at their default.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-k, \-\-key <key>
Dotted path to a single value, such as \fIdownload.default_directory\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-raw
Dump the file as stored instead of summarising.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-secure
Read \fISecure Preferences\fP instead.
